{"step_index":133,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T15:01:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T17:01:44+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T17:01:44+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity_handoff.py`\nTotal Lines: 348\nTotal Bytes: 15551\nShowing lines 101 to 200\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n101: \n102: # ── admissibility ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n103: #\n104: # An answer is compiled as the *returned file*, helper lemmas included — pasting\n105: # only the proof body back into the original, as the model campaign did, drops\n106: # every lemma a real proof needs and turns a correct proof into \"unresolved\".\n107: #\n108: # Compiling the returned file is only sound if nothing in it can change what is\n109: # being proved. The checks below close the routes that exist in Lean for that:\n110: # editing `Candidate` or anything it elaborates against; extending its term past\n111: # where it ended (a term does not stop at a newline); re-declaring `Candidate` or\n112: # the target inside a namespace; adding `variable` hypotheses the target silently\n113: # absorbs; redefining the tokens `Candidate` parses as; and bypassing the kernel.\n114: # The target's type is then re-checked by Lean itself, and the axiom audit rejects\n115: # `sorryAx` and anything non-standard.\n116: \n117: _CMD_START = (\"theorem\", \"lemma\", \"def\", \"abbrev\", \"example\", \"instance\", \"open\",\n118:               \"set_option\", \"attribute\", \"noncomputable\", \"private\", \"protected\",\n119:               \"@[\", \"#check\", \"#print\", \"structure\", \"inductive\", \"class\")\n120: \n121: _FORBIDDEN_CMD = re.compile(\n122:     r\"(?m)^\\s*(?:(?:private|protected|noncomputable|local|scoped)\\s+)*\"\n123:     r\"(namespace|section|variable|universe|notation\\w*|\n<truncated 1905 bytes>\nn): may the returned file be compiled as an answer at all?\"\"\"\n162:     orig, ret = _norm(original), _norm(returned)\n163:     pre = _prefix(orig)\n164:     if pre is None:\n165:         return False, \"original challenge is malformed\"\n166:     if not ret.startswith(pre):\n167:         return False, \"statement changed: text above the first theorem differs\"\n168:     rest = ret[len(pre):]\n169:     if rest and not rest.startswith(\"\\n\"):\n170:         return False, \"statement changed: Candidate's last line was extended\"\n171:     code = _strip_comments(rest)\n172:     head = code.lstrip()\n173:     if head and not head.startswith(_CMD_START):\n174:         return False, \"statement changed: Candidate continues past its original end\"\n175:     m = _FORBIDDEN_CMD.search(code)\n176:     if m:\n177:         return False, f\"forbidden command `{m.group(1)}`\"\n178:     m = _FORBIDDEN_TOKEN.search(code)\n179:     if m:\n180:         return False, f\"forbidden construct `{m.group(0)}`\"\n181:     return True, \"\"\n182: \n183: \n184: def lint_text(text: str, original=None):\n185:     \"\"\"(ok, reason) for any Lean file an agent asks to elaborate.\n186: \n187:     A challenge file is held to `structural_check` against its original. Any\n188:     other file (scratch lemmas) gets the same code-execution screen plus an\n189:     import whitelist, since `import` is the other way to pull in code.\n190:     \"\"\"\n191:     if original is not None:\n192:         return structural_check(original, text)\n193:     code = _strip_comments(_norm(text))\n194:     for m in re.finditer(r\"(?m)^\\s*import\\s+(\\S+)\", code):\n195:         if m.group(1) not in _ALLOWED_IMPORTS:\n196:             return False, f\"import `{m.group(1)}` is not allowed\"\n197:     m = _FORBIDDEN_CMD.search(code)\n198:     if m:\n199:         return False, f\"forbidden